This folder packages the Rockbox simulator as an Android app: the device
skin, buttons and clickwheel as on the desktop, running on a phone. It is
unrelated to the older Rockbox-as-an-application port in /android.

The simulator is built as libmain.so and started by SDL2's SDLActivity.
Codecs and plugins ship in the APK as libraries next to it, because Android
won't run code from app storage (see uisimulator/common/load_code-sim.c).
The simulated disk is the phone's shared storage (/sdcard), so the app asks
for "All files access" on first start. Rockbox's own files (.rockbox) are
kept in /sdcard/Rockbox/.rockbox instead of at the root (see
uisimulator/common/filesystem-sim.c), unpacked there on first run and after
updates.

Only arm64 (aarch64) is supported.

* Prerequisites

- Android SDK with build-tools and platforms;android-35
- Android NDK r27 or later
- A JDK
- SDL2 source (2.32 or later), built and installed for Android:

    cmake -S SDL2-2.32.10 -B sdl2-android -G Ninja \
        -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=$ANDROID_NDK_PATH/build/cmake/android.toolchain.cmake \
        -DANDROID_ABI=arm64-v8a -DANDROID_PLATFORM=26 -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
        -DSDL_STATIC=OFF -DSDL_TEST=OFF -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=$PWD/sdl2-android/prefix
    cmake --build sdl2-android && cmake --install sdl2-android

* Build instructions

    export ANDROID_SDK_PATH=~/Android/Sdk
    export ANDROID_NDK_PATH=~/Android/Sdk/ndk/<version>
    export ANDROID_SDL2_PREFIX=/path/to/sdl2-android/prefix
    export ANDROID_SDL2_SOURCE=/path/to/SDL2-2.32.10

    mkdir build-android && cd build-android
    ../tools/configure --target=ipodvideo --type=s --android-sim
    make && make install
    ../uisimulator/android/build-apk.sh
    adb install -r rockbox-sim.apk

The simulator's output is written to stdout.txt in the app's private
files directory:

    adb shell run-as org.rockbox.sim cat files/stdout.txt
